		<ITag type="e">
			<_id type="a">GUID 32c02bf4-a553-4d79-b28a-442c7f6ef0e7</_id>
			<_name type="a">RCV_RECEIVE_INVALID</_name>
			<_modifiedTimeWeak type="a">1.2.1990::0:0:0</_modifiedTimeWeak>
			<_description type="p"><IDescription type="e">
				<_textRTF type="a">{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1031{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Arial;}}%0D
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fs20 This communication attribute defines how the receivers wants to respond when an invalid value for a data element is received. The configuration of this attribute is optional for each data element defined in the \i TransportedInterface\i0 . The value specified her is valid for every receiver as long as the receivers don't overwrite it.\par%0D
\par%0D
\b Related References:\b0\par%0D
- AUTOSAR Specifiaction Virtual Functional Bus\par%0D
- Tag &lt;DATA_RCV_RECEIVE_INVALID&gt; defined for the stereotype \i &lt;TransportedInterface&gt;\i0\par%0D
}%0D
</_textRTF>
			</IDescription>
			</_description>
			<_modifiedTime type="a">1.2.1990::0:0:0</_modifiedTime>
			<_typeOf type="r">
				<IHandle type="e">
					<_hm2Class type="a">IType</_hm2Class>
					<_hid type="a">GUID a11e1926-6247-4bf7-8454-e21c36161ab7</_hid>
				</IHandle>
			</_typeOf>
			<_isOrdered type="a">0</_isOrdered>
		</ITag>
		<ITag type="e">
			<_id type="a">GUID 6f2f520d-3184-41ca-b528-502f947c0b32</_id>
			<_name type="a">RCV_TIME_FOR_RESYNC</_name>
			<_modifiedTimeWeak type="a">1.2.1990::0:0:0</_modifiedTimeWeak>
			<_description type="p"><IDescription type="e">
				<_textRTF type="a">{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1031{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Arial;}}%0D
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fs20 This communication attribute defines the receivers' time allowed for resynchronization of data values after current data is lost e.g. an ECU reset. The configuration of this attribute is optional for each data element defined in the \i TransportedInterface\i0 . The value specified her is valid for every receiver as long as the receivers don't overwrite it.\par%0D
\par%0D
\b Related References:\b0\par%0D
- AUTOSAR Specifiaction Virtual Functional Bus\par%0D
- Tag &lt;DATA_RCV_TIME_FOR_RESYNC&gt; defined for the stereotype \i &lt;TransportedInterface&gt;\i0\par%0D
}%0D
</_textRTF>
			</IDescription>
			</_description>
			<_modifiedTime type="a">1.2.1990::0:0:0</_modifiedTime>
			<_typeOf type="r">
				<IHandle type="e">
					<_hm2Class type="a">IType</_hm2Class>
					<_hid type="a">GUID ab632560-f95c-4a8c-9210-81a5136ea7a1</_hid>
				</IHandle>
			</_typeOf>
			<_isOrdered type="a">0</_isOrdered>
		</ITag>
		<ITag type="e">
			<_id type="a">GUID 0fa857ff-7b21-4507-812f-584161dea513</_id>
			<_name type="a">RCV_ALIVE_TIMEOUT</_name>
			<_modifiedTimeWeak type="a">1.2.1990::0:0:0</_modifiedTimeWeak>
			<_description type="p"><IDescription type="e">
				<_textRTF type="a">{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1031{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Arial;}}%0D
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fs20 With this communication attribute the receiver specifies the maximum period of time it may take to receive the current data until it becomes outdated. The configuration of this attribute is optional for each data element defined in the \i TransportedInterface\i0 . The value specified her is valid for every receiver as long as the receivers don't overwrite it.\par%0D
\par%0D
\b Related References:\b0\par%0D
- AUTOSAR Specifiaction Virtual Functional Bus\par%0D
- Tag &lt;DATA_RCV_ALIVE_TIMEOUT&gt; defined for the stereotype \i &lt;TransportedInterface&gt;\i0\par%0D
\par%0D
}%0D
</_textRTF>
			</IDescription>
			</_description>
			<_modifiedTime type="a">1.2.1990::0:0:0</_modifiedTime>
			<_typeOf type="r">
