			<_name type="a">RCV_RECEIVER_QUEUELENGTH</_name>
			<_modifiedTimeWeak type="a">1.2.1990::0:0:0</_modifiedTimeWeak>
			<_description type="p"><IDescription type="e">
				<_textRTF type="a">{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1031{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Arial;}}%0D
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fs20 With this communication attribute the receiver specifies the size of the queue where event element are queued. The configuration of this attribute is mandatory for each event element defined in the \i TransportedInterface\i0 . The value specified her is valid for every receiver as long as the receivers don't overwrite it.\par%0D
\par%0D
\b Related References:\b0\par%0D
- AUTOSAR Specification Virtual Functional Bus\par%0D
- Tag &lt;EVENT_RCV_RECEIVER_QUEUELENGTH&gt; defined for the stereotype \i &lt;TransportedInterface&gt;\i0\par%0D
