			<_modifiedTimeWeak type="a">1.2.1990::0:0:0</_modifiedTimeWeak>
			<_description type="p"><IDescription type="e">
				<_textRTF type="a">{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1031{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Arial;}}%0D
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fs20 With this communication attribute the sender specifies the size of the input queue for the mode switch notifications towards a mode machine. The configuration of this attribute is mandatory for each mode element defined in the \i TransportedInterface\i0 . \par%0D
\par%0D
\b Related References:\b0\par%0D
- AUTOSAR Specification Virtual Functional Bus\par%0D
- Tag &lt;MODE_SND_MODE_QUEUELENGTH&gt; defined for the stereotype \i &lt;TransportedInterface&gt;\i0\par%0D
\par%0D
\par%0D
}%0D
</_textRTF>
