				</IHandle>
			</_typeOf>
			<_isOrdered type="a">0</_isOrdered>
		</ITag>
		<ITag type="e">
			<_id type="a">GUID 27510944-38e1-44b3-aebb-228ef14221a7</_id>
			<_name type="a">SND_TX_ACK_TIMEOUT</_name>
			<_modifiedTimeWeak type="a">1.2.1990::0:0:0</_modifiedTimeWeak>
			<_description type="p"><IDescription type="e">
				<_textRTF type="a">{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1031{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Arial;}}%0D
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fs20 This communication attribute defines whether the sender has to be informed when the mode has been sent correctly. The configuration of this attribute is optional for each mode element defined in the \i TransportedInterface\i0 .\par%0D
\par%0D
\b Related References:\b0\par%0D
- AUTOSAR Specifiaction Virtual Functional Bus\par%0D
- Tag &lt;EVENT_SND_TX_ACK_TIMEOUT&gt; defined for the stereotype \i &lt;TransportedInterface&gt;\i0\par%0D
}%0D
</_textRTF>
			</IDescription>
			</_description>
			<_modifiedTime type="a">1.2.1990::0:0:0</_modifiedTime>
			<_typeOf type="r">
				<IHandle type="e">
					<_hm2Class type="a">IType</_hm2Class>
					<_hid type="a">GUID ab632560-f95c-4a8c-9210-81a5136ea7a1</_hid>
				</IHandle>
			</_typeOf>
			<_isOrdered type="a">0</_isOrdered>
		</ITag>
		<IStereotype type="e">
			<_id type="a">GUID 980a3bce-31bc-429d-882f-5d3ee351012c</_id>
			<_myState type="a">8192</_myState>
			<_name type="a">ModeGroup</_name>
			<_modifiedTimeWeak type="a">1.23.2020::10:54:16</_modifiedTimeWeak>
			<_description type="p"><IDescription type="e">
				<_textRTF type="a">{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1031{\fonttbl{\f0\fswiss\fprq2\fcharset0 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Arial;}}%0D
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\lang1033\f0\fs20 This stereotype is applicable to types that are used to declared \i &lt;&lt;Mode&gt;&gt;\i0  attributes within the \i TransportedInterface. \i0 It identifies mode information, as introduced by AUTOSAR.\lang1031\f1\par%0D
}%0D
</_textRTF>
			</IDescription>
			</_description>
			<_modifiedTime type="a">1.2.1990::0:0:0</_modifiedTime>
			<_m2Classes type="c">
				<IRPYRawContainer type="e">
					<size type="a">1</size>
					<value>Type</value>
				</IRPYRawContainer>
			</_m2Classes>
		</IStereotype>
		<IStereotype type="e">
			<_id type="a">GUID a34076ad-225b-4e76-9ec8-6209db85795b</_id>
			<_myState type="a">8192</_myState>
			<_name type="a">Runnable</_name>
			<_modifiedTimeWeak type="a">1.23.2020::10:54:16</_modifiedTimeWeak>
			<_description type="p"><IDescription type="e">
				<_textRTF type="a">{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1031{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Arial;}}%0D
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fs20 A \i &lt;&lt;Runnable&gt;&gt;\i0  method identifies a class method that is invoked by the RTE on the basis of RTE-Events. The \i Runnable \i0 is supposed to be executed in the thread that is assigned to the \i Allocatable \i0 it is part of.\par%0D
\par%0D
\b Related References:\b0\par%0D
- AUTOSAR Specifiaction of RTE\par%0D
}%0D
</_textRTF>
			</IDescription>
			</_description>
			<_modifiedTime type="a">1.2.1990::0:0:0</_modifiedTime>
			<_lastID type="a">2</_lastID>
