		<ITag type="e">
			<_id type="a">GUID e829d2da-8bac-47b5-9d77-ceb099616db9</_id>
			<_name type="a">DATA_SND_INIT_VALUE</_name>
			<_modifiedTimeWeak type="a">1.2.1990::0:0:0</_modifiedTimeWeak>
			<_description type="p"><IDescription type="e">
				<_textRTF type="a">{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1031{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Arial;}}%0D
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fs20 This group attribute defines the default initial value for all data elements with the stereotype \i &lt;Data&gt;\i0  defined in the \i TransportedInterface.\i0  The value defined here can be overwritten by the value defined for a specific data element. The configuration of this attribute within the definition of the \i TransportedInterface\i0  is optional.\par%0D
\par%0D
\b Related References:\b0\par%0D
- AUTOSAR Specifiaction Virtual Functional Bus\par%0D
- Tag &lt;SND_INIT_VALUE&gt; defined for the stereotype \i &lt;data&gt;\i0\par%0D
}%0D
</_textRTF>
			</IDescription>
			</_description>
			<_modifiedTime type="a">1.2.1990::0:0:0</_modifiedTime>
			<_typeOf type="r">
				<IHandle type="e">
					<_hm2Class type="a">IType</_hm2Class>
					<_hid type="a">GUID cce07483-f75f-4253-be3e-fbfb8246d2fb</_hid>
				</IHandle>
			</_typeOf>
			<_isOrdered type="a">0</_isOrdered>
		</ITag>
		<ITag type="e">
			<_id type="a">GUID fca19ec1-73f5-46fb-a131-fab154c8af4f</_id>
			<_name type="a">DATA_SND_CAN_INVALIDATE</_name>
			<_modifiedTimeWeak type="a">1.2.1990::0:0:0</_modifiedTimeWeak>
			<_description type="p"><IDescription type="e">
				<_textRTF type="a">{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1031{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Arial;}}%0D
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fs20 This group attribute defines whether the sender can invalidate a data element. This attribute may define a default value for all data elements with the stereotype \i &lt;Data&gt;\i0  defined in the \i TransportedInterface.\i0  The value defined here can be overwritten by the value defined for a specific data element. The configuration of this attribute within the definition of the \i TransportedInterface \i0 is optional.\par%0D
\par%0D
\b Related References:\b0\par%0D
- AUTOSAR Specifiaction Virtual Functional Bus\par%0D
- Tag &lt;SND_CAN_INVALIDATE&gt; defined for the stereotype \i &lt;data&gt;\i0\par%0D
}%0D
</_textRTF>
			</IDescription>
			</_description>
			<_modifiedTime type="a">1.2.1990::0:0:0</_modifiedTime>
			<_typeOf type="r">
