		<IType type="e">
			<_id type="a">GUID 2ab7577f-c3d0-4d07-b480-5866118f53cf</_id>
			<_myState type="a">8192</_myState>
			<_name type="a">A2TCallTrigger</_name>
			<_modifiedTimeWeak type="a">1.23.2020::10:54:16</_modifiedTimeWeak>
			<_description type="p"><IDescription type="e">
				<_textRTF type="a">{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1031{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Arial;}{\f1\fswiss\fprq2\fcharset0 Arial;}}%0D
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fs20 This enumerator type defines the possible events raised by a \i &lt;&lt;call&gt;&gt;\i0  operation defined within a \i TransportedInterface\i0 . Selectable literals are:\b\par%0D
\b0\par%0D
\lang1033\b\i\f1 OpertationInvoked:\b0\i0  A runnable entity on the client side is triggered by the RTE in response to a received request from the client to execute the operation. Corresponding RTE-Event is \i OperationInvokedEvent\i0  and is relevant for client-server communication.\par%0D
NB: This event is no more selectable because it is implicily put when TI server name equal to class function name which realize the interface.\lang1031\f0\par%0D
\par%0D
\lang1033\b\f1 A\i synchronousServerCallReturns:\b0  \i0 A runnable entity on the client side is triggered to process the result of the asynchronous server call operation. Corresponding RTE-Event is A\i synchronousServerCallReturnsEvent \i0 and is relevant for client-server communication.\par%0D
\lang1031\f0\par%0D
\b Related References:\b0\par%0D
- AUTOSAR Specification of RTE\par%0D
}%0D
</_textRTF>
			</IDescription>
			</_description>
			<_modifiedTime type="a">1.2.1990::0:0:0</_modifiedTime>
			<_lastID type="a">3</_lastID>
			<_kind type="a">Enumeration</_kind>
			<AggregatesList type="e">
				<value>GUID 7e546c7e-ec1f-4443-9357-6e425e576732</value>
				<value>GUID 1e23aafd-0b0e-47a0-ad15-8a3a6572868b</value>
			</AggregatesList>
		</IType>
		<IEnumerationLiteral type="e">
			<_id type="a">GUID 7e546c7e-ec1f-4443-9357-6e425e576732</_id>
			<_name type="a">AsynchronousServerCallReturn</_name>
