		<IType type="e">
			<_id type="a">GUID c2258d7b-c82f-4bff-9f5c-04e876856eba</_id>
			<_myState type="a">8192</_myState>
			<_name type="a">A2TDataTrigger</_name>
			<_modifiedTimeWeak type="a">1.23.2020::10:54:16</_modifiedTimeWeak>
			<_description type="p"><IDescription type="e">
				<_textRTF type="a">{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1031{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Arial;}{\f1\fswiss\fprq2\fcharset0 Arial;}}%0D
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fs20 This enumerator type defines the possible events raised by a \i &lt;&lt;data&gt;&gt;\i0  attribute defined within a \i TransportedInterface\i0 . Selectable literals are:\b\par%0D
\b0\par%0D
\lang1033\b\i\f1 DataReceived:\b0\i0  A runnable entity on the receiver side is triggered by the RTE to receive and process a data attribute defined in the \i TransportedInterface\i0 . Corresponding RTE-Event is \i DataReceivedEvent\i0  and is relevant for sender-receiver communication.\lang1031\f0\par%0D
\par%0D
\lang1033\b\i\f1 DataReceivedError:\b0\i0  A runnable entity on the receiver side is triggered by the RTE to collect the error status of a data attribute defined in the \i TransportedInterface\i0 . Corresponding RTE-Event is \i DataReceiveErrorEvent\i0  and is relevant for sender-receiver communication.\lang1031\f0\par%0D
\par%0D
\lang1033\b\i\f1 DataSendCompleted:\b0\i0  A runnable entity on the provider side is triggered by the RTE to receive transmission acknowledgement notifications for a data attribute defined in the \i TransportedInterface\i0 . Corresponding RTE-Event is \i DataSendCompletedEvent\i0  and is relevant for sender-receiver communication.\lang1031\f0\par%0D
\par%0D
\b Related References:\b0\par%0D
- AUTOSAR Specification of RTE\par%0D
\par%0D
}%0D
</_textRTF>
			</IDescription>
