			<_name type="a">A2TInvalidHandling</_name>
			<_modifiedTimeWeak type="a">1.23.2020::10:54:16</_modifiedTimeWeak>
			<_description type="p"><IDescription type="e">
				<_textRTF type="a">{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1031{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Arial;}{\f1\fswiss\fprq2\fcharset0 Arial;}}%0D
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fs20 This enumerator type defines the possible ways to handle the reception of an invalid data or event. Selectable literals are:\b\par%0D
\b0\par%0D
\lang1033\b\i\f1 Keep:\b0\i0  The invalid value is kept as it was received.\lang1031\f0\par%0D
\par%0D
\lang1033\b\i\f1 Replace:\b0\i0  The invalid value is replaced by a valid one as defined by the user.\lang1031\f0\par%0D
\par%0D
\b Related References:\b0\par%0D
- AUTOSAR Specification of RTE\par%0D
}%0D
</_textRTF>
