		<ITag type="e">
			<_id type="a">GUID 7697a193-3b85-4fe9-9ece-0a3fbe178752</_id>
			<_name type="a">JustifiedRules</_name>
			<_modifiedTimeWeak type="a">1.2.1990::0:0:0</_modifiedTimeWeak>
			<_description type="p"><IDescription type="e">
				<_textRTF type="a">{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1251\deff0\deflang1026{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset204{\*\fname Arial;}Arial CYR;}}%0D
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\lang1033\fs20 This tag is used to disable/justify specific model checker rule(s).\par%0D
It should contain list of strings in the following format:\par%0D
&lt;RuleID&gt;:&lt;Author&gt;-&lt;Justification&gt;\par%0D
Example:\par%0D
Mdl.Gen.Obj.Rule.2:avincha-Analysis on the risk was done by the project and it was decided that this rule should be disable on this element.\lang1026\f1\par%0D
}%0D
</_textRTF>
			</IDescription>
			</_description>
			<_modifiedTime type="a">1.2.1990::0:0:0</_modifiedTime>
			<_typeOf type="r">
				<IHandle type="e">
					<_hm2Class type="a">IType</_hm2Class>
					<_hsubsystem type="a">PredefinedTypes</_hsubsystem>
					<_hname type="a">RhpString</_hname>
					<_hid type="a">GUID ae5e3720-4e3e-40f1-9346-9a8b4e501f35</_hid>
				</IHandle>
			</_typeOf>
			<_multiplicity type="a">1..*</_multiplicity>
			<_isOrdered type="a">0</_isOrdered>
		</ITag>
		<IStereotype type="e">
			<_id type="a">GUID ff96cd6b-c5d4-443e-a9d1-bf181e501cc4</_id>
			<_myState type="a">8192</_myState>
			<_name type="a">Namespace</_name>
			<_modifiedTimeWeak type="a">1.23.2020::10:54:16</_modifiedTimeWeak>
			<_description type="p"><IDescription type="e">
				<_textRTF type="a">{\rtf1\fbidis\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1036{\fonttbl{\f0\fswiss\fprq2\fcharset0 Arial;}{\f1\fmodern\fprq1\fcharset0 Courier New;}{\f2\fnil\fcharset0 Arial;}}%0D
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\ltrpar\sa200\lang1033\f0\fs20 Purpose of namespace is to hold a logical grouping of unique identifiers or symbol.\par%0D
Inside a namespace, Package and class are identified by their name. For this reason, their name shall be unique in the namespace.\par%0D
In addition to its name, a namespace gets two tags (tags are optional fields entered by the designer):\par%0D
\pard\ltrpar\fi-360\li873\sa200\f1 o\tab\f0 A text, \ldblquote ShortName\rdblquote . This tag is by default the name of the namespace in upper case.\par%0D
\f1 o\tab\f0 A Boolean, \ldblquote InheritsPrefix\rdblquote . This tag is by default true.\par%0D
\pard\ltrpar\sa200 At generation time, a prefix is used earlier the definition of any global symbols.\par%0D
If \ldblquote InheritedPrefix\rdblquote  is false, the prefix is \ldblquote ShortName\rdblquote .\par%0D
If not, the prefix is: (the Prefix from the parent namespace) + \ldblquote ShortName\rdblquote .\par%0D
\pard\ltrpar\lang1036\f2\par%0D
}%0D
</_textRTF>
			</IDescription>
			</_description>
			<_modifiedTime type="a">1.2.1990::0:0:0</_modifiedTime>
			<_m2Classes type="c">
				<IRPYRawContainer type="e">
